    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0119" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/695: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-07T19:00:00-05:00">December 7, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>656. The Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="61a" xml:id="d132-f1"/> just
                    requested me to transmit the following message for President Roosevelt from
                    President Prado: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>President Prado desires to make known to the United States and especially
                            to President Roosevelt that the attitude of Peru is one of entire
                            cooperation in giving to the United States any assistance or support in
                            measures which it may be necessary to take to meet the situation in the
                            Pacific.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I hope that I may have a telegraphic acknowledgement of this message.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d132-f1" n="61a" xml:id="d132-f1-content">
                <p>Alfredo Solf y Muro.</p>
            </note>
